Lina: Quick thread — I'm doing a tight refresh of the 'Hello Thicket' quickstart. Goals: unify env var naming, add a one-file Rust example (was requested by infra), fix a broken anchor to /deploy/production#blue-green, and update JS streaming snippet to new async iterator API.
Mark: Sounds good. What env var are we standardizing on? We already have two variants floating: REDWOOD_KEY and RW_API_KEY.
Lina: Proposal: RWINFER_KEY (short and explicit). We'll include a small migration note for REDWOOD_KEY/RW_API_KEY.
Yusuf: I ran the sample and hit 401 — README referenced RW_API_KEY but samples used REDWOOD_KEY. I'll update samples/.env.example, docker-compose, and the launch script.
Lina: Thanks. Also add a tiny script scripts/migrate_env.sh that sets RWINFER_KEY from any of the old vars if present. Keep it idempotent.
Mark: CI flagged node v16 in the docker image. Streaming JS example now assumes async iterator which needs node >=18. I'll add engines: {"node": ">=18"} in samples/package.json and a short note in README.
Priya: For the Rust example, keep it minimal (reqwest + tokio) and show the Authorization header pattern. Example: ```rust
// hello_thicket.rs
use reqwest::Client;
#[tokio::main] async fn main() {
  let k = std::env::var("RWINFER_KEY").unwrap();
  let cli = Client::new();
  let r = cli.post("https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate")
    .bearer_auth(k)
    .json(&serde_json::json!({"model":"thicket-mini","prompt":"Hi"}))
    .send().await.unwrap();
  println!("{}", r.text().await.unwrap());
}
```
Priya: Keeping it short — uses common crates. Add a small note about installing tokio/reqwest.
Yusuf: Also update the JS streaming snippet to the new pattern: 
```js
for await (const part of client.streamGenerate({ model: 'thicket-mini', prompt })) {
  process.stdout.write(part.chunk);
}
```
